1. DEFINITIONS AND GENERAL SCOPE
--------------------------------

For this notice:

- "Original Materials" means original source code, scripts, configuration,
  documentation, interface code, schemas, build logic, original annotations,
  and other materials created for this project by Scorpascal or by a
  contributor who has the right to license them.
- "Archived Materials" means copies, snapshots, conversions, records, source
  recoveries, metadata, or other materials collected from YOJ or another
  external source and preserved by the project.
- "Third-Party Materials" means material created by a person or organization
  other than the person granting the applicable license, or material subject
  to a separate license, contract, platform rule, institutional rule, or other
  restriction.
- "Repository" means the public RUC_YOJ repository and its public GitHub Pages
  deployment, as applicable.

The MIT license in section 3 applies to Original Materials only. It does not
automatically apply to Archived Materials or Third-Party Materials. A file may
contain both original and third-party portions; in that situation, the MIT
license applies only to the separable original portions for which the relevant
rights holder has authority to grant it.


2. ORIGINAL PROJECT MATERIALS
-----------------------------

Unless another notice applies, the following types of material are intended to
be Original Materials when they were created by Scorpascal or by an authorized
contributor:

- repository source code and scripts written specifically for RUC_YOJ;
- crawling, synchronization, parsing, conversion, normalization, validation,
