  and project-specific configuration;
- project-specific data-processing logic, schemas, generated-file builders,
  report builders, and automation configuration;
- README text, method documents, operating instructions, and other project
  documentation authored by the project author;
- original explanatory notes, annotations, index descriptions, and editorial
  material authored for this repository;
- original solution code authored by Scorpascal, where Scorpascal owns the
  copyright or otherwise has the right to license that code;
- original metadata structures, validation rules, status projections, build
  logic, and other software components created for the project.

These examples describe categories, not a blanket claim over every byte in a
directory. Originality and licensing authority must still be determined from
the relevant file, its history, its attribution, and any upstream source.


