4. PUBLIC REPOSITORY CONTENT AND DIRECTORY BOUNDARIES
------------------------------------------------------

The public repository currently combines software, documentation, archived
content, derived data, and a public web interface. The following directory
guidance is intended to make those boundaries explicit:

4.1 Software and project documentation

The following areas are primarily intended to contain Original Materials,
subject to the file-specific and mixed-content qualifications in this notice:

- tools/ contains project maintenance, capture, conversion, validation,
  auditing, publication, scheduling, and deployment scripts.
- services/traffic-worker/ contains the project-specific traffic service,
  schema, tests, and deployment documentation. Cloudflare products, runtime
  components, and external services remain subject to their own terms.
- docs/ contains the static public site and quick-submit interface. The
  interface code and project-specific presentation logic may be Original
  Materials, while text, images, links, and problem content displayed by the
  site may be Archived Materials or Third-Party Materials.
- method/ contains project procedures, operating notes, repository conventions,
  and compliance guidance. External quotations, references, or copied
  upstream material remain subject to their own rights.
- the root README.md and project-specific configuration contain a mixture of
  original documentation, generated summaries, links, and upstream-derived
  facts. Only the original portions are covered by the MIT license.

4.2 Archived solutions and problem pages

- 代码库/ may contain complete source files, submission-shaped source files,
  metadata, accepted-submission references, and recovered source material.
  A source file is not automatically Original Materials merely because it is
  stored in this directory. Code authored by another person, recovered from
  an online judge, or copied from an upstream submission remains subject to
  the rights and terms applicable to that code.
- 题解/ may contain problem-page snapshots, converted text, formulas, sample
  input and output, links to original pages, locally referenced images,
  original annotations, and other mixed content. The project-authored
  conversion or annotation logic may be original, but the underlying problem
  content is not automatically relicensed.
- assets and image files may be downloaded, copied, or referenced from an
  online judge or another source. Their presence does not grant permission to
  reproduce, modify, distribute, or use them commercially.

4.3 Data, reports, and generated public artifacts

The following areas may contain project-authored schemas, transformation logic,
status projections, or generated presentation structures together with
upstream-derived or externally observed values:

- data/;
- docs/data/;
- staging/;
- .yoj-sync/;
- generated tables, catalogs, reports, JSON records, and status summaries
  committed elsewhere in the repository.

The project may license its original schema, selection logic, transformation
code, validation logic, and editorial annotations under the MIT license where
it owns those rights. That grant does not automatically relicense the
underlying problem text, images, submission records, platform responses,
external identifiers, or other upstream-derived material.

The directory list above is descriptive rather than exhaustive. A new file
must be classified by its contents and applicable notices, not by its
location alone.


