9. AUTOMATED SUBMISSION AND ONLINE-JUDGE USE
---------------------------------------------

Some RUC_YOJ components may assist with opening online-judge pages, preparing
or copying source code, submitting source code, synchronizing accepted
submissions, checking online status, or interacting with publicly accessible
online-judge interfaces.

Use of such functionality is entirely at the user's discretion and risk.
This license does not represent or guarantee that automated or assisted use
is permitted by any particular online judge, course, institution, contest,
browser, network, or service.

Users are responsible for complying with the applicable service's terms, rate
limits, authentication rules, anti-abuse controls, access restrictions,
course requirements, and other policies. Users must not use the project to
bypass access controls, expose private credentials, evade a judge's rules,
submit unauthorized work, or interfere with a service.

The project authors are not responsible for account restrictions, submission
errors, duplicate submissions, lost work, incorrect submissions, service
interruptions, rate-limit consequences, academic penalties, or other results
of using these tools.


10. STATUS, ACCURACY, AND VERIFICATION DISCLAIMER
--------------------------------------------------

RUC_YOJ records and displays project-specific states such as PUBLIC_READY,
RAW_CAPTURED, TOPIC_CAPTURED, ONLINE_ACCEPTED, NO_LOCAL_AC,
ONLINE_SKIPPED_SUBMIT_FORM_NOT_FOUND, YOJ_PUBLIC, and
NOT_IN_CURRENT_PUBLIC_INDEX. These labels describe evidence and validation
available to the project at a particular time and are not warranties.

In particular:

- PUBLIC_READY is a project publication gate, not a guarantee of future
  online availability, correctness, or permission to reuse upstream content.
- ONLINE_ACCEPTED records an observed online-judge result; it is not a
  perpetual guarantee that the same source will remain accepted.
- RAW_CAPTURED and TOPIC_CAPTURED describe archival progress, not correctness
  or a recommendation to submit the material.
- YOJ_PUBLIC and NOT_IN_CURRENT_PUBLIC_INDEX describe an observed public-index
  snapshot; they do not determine copyright ownership or authorize copying.
- NO_LOCAL_AC and skipped-verification states describe the project's evidence
  boundary, not the quality or legality of the underlying material.

No representation or warranty is made that repository information is complete,
current, accurate, suitable for a particular course, accepted by the current
version of an online judge, free from parsing or synchronization errors,
identical to the current upstream problem statement, or suitable for
assessment or production use.

Historical records, hashes, timestamps, page-load counts, traffic snapshots,
source links, and generated reports may become stale or unavailable. Users
should verify important information against the applicable current source.


11. SECURITY, PRIVACY, CREDENTIALS, AND HOSTED SERVICES
--------------------------------------------------------

The project is designed so that passwords, private authentication tokens,
session credentials, browser cookies, keychain secrets, API tokens, and
similar private credentials should not be committed to the public repository.
Users are responsible for protecting their own credentials and for reviewing
configuration before deploying or modifying the project.

The project authors accept no responsibility for credentials, personal data,
private information, or account access that a user intentionally or
accidentally exposes while using, modifying, deploying, or redistributing the
project.

The traffic-statistics components may process public page-load events and may
use a project-defined identifier, time zone, daily series, or aggregate
counter. A page-load counter is not a verified unique-visitor count. Unless
separately documented, project traffic statistics should not be interpreted
as a complete audience measurement or as proof of a particular person's
activity.

The public Pages site, traffic worker, database, GitHub Actions, external
online judge, Cloudflare services, and other hosted systems may be changed,
limited, interrupted, or discontinued by their operators. A license to
Original Materials does not grant control over any hosted service.


